<Id>XuiHtmlElement1</Id>
<Width>544.000000</Width>
<Height>312.000000</Height>
<Position>24.000000,56.000000,0.000000</Position>
<Text>&lt;font color="#000000" size=11&gt;

There are a few different options for dealing with text in your &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scenes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.
The &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Text&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control is the most basic of them, giving you some simple font and color choices.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

The next step up is a &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Label&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control, which has the capability of being skinned with a &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Visual&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.
This means that all of your font settings are pulling from the skin file, allowing you to have a more consistent standard from page to page.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

There is also an &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Edit&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control for situations that require the user to input something.
To type text into this &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Edit&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control using the keyboard, first enable the 'Tools &gt; Keyboard Input' menu option.</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlElement>
